# ── FAILURE DIAGNOSIS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Error: run_experiment: SandboxRuntimeError: RunPod sandbox is selected but
#   SSH private key was not found: \Users\aayushbaniya\.ssh\reprolab_runpod_ed25519
#
# Root cause — THREE-layer bug chain:
#   1. A prior session or machine configuration left
#        REPROLAB_RUNPOD_SSH_KEY_PATH=\Users\aayushbaniya\.ssh\reprolab_runpod_ed25519
#      in the shell/process environment of the backend server process.
#      This value refers to a different user (aayushbaniya) and has no drive
#      letter (\ instead of C:\).
#
#   2. live_runs.py::_subprocess_env() builds the run subprocess environment
#      via `env = {**os.environ}` then loads .env with `if k not in env`.
#      That condition means .env values can NEVER override process-level env
#      vars — the stale aayushbaniya path propagated unchanged into every
#      spawned run subprocess.
#
#   3. Inside the subprocess, `get_settings()` reads settings.runpod_ssh_key_path
#      from os.environ (stale value wins over .env) and caches it. Every call
#      to run_experiment → ensure_runpod_available() checks that path →
#      Path("\Users\aayushbaniya\...").exists() → False → SandboxRuntimeError.
#
# Correct state confirmed:
#   .env REPROLAB_RUNPOD_SSH_KEY_PATH = C:/Users/armaa/.ssh/reprolab_runpod_ed25519
#   SSH key at that path: EXISTS (419 bytes, created 2026-05-24 16:32)
#   Stale path \Users\aayushbaniya\...: DOES NOT EXIST on this machine
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── FIXES APPLIED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Fix 1 — backend/services/events/live_runs.py (line 335):
#   Changed: if k and k not in env:
#   To:      if k and (k.startswith("REPROLAB_") or k not in env):
#   Effect:  REPROLAB_* keys from .env are always authoritative over stale
#            inherited process-level env vars.  Non-REPROLAB keys (API keys,
#            PATH, etc.) retain the existing "shell export > .env" priority.
#
# Fix 2 — killed stale subprocess (PID 32076):
#   The already-running subprocess had the wrong path in its in-memory
#   os.environ and a cached Settings instance — no file change can fix that
#   from outside the process.  The subprocess was terminated so the run can
#   be resumed cleanly with the patched live_runs.py in effect.
#   Command: taskkill //PID 32076 //F   (exit 0)
#
# Action required by operator:
#   Resume or restart the run via the UI or CLI.  The new subprocess will
#   inherit REPROLAB_RUNPOD_SSH_KEY_PATH=C:/Users/armaa/.ssh/reprolab_runpod_ed25519
#   from .env (Fix 1 guarantees .env wins), which resolves to the existing key.
#   The backend server does NOT need to be restarted — live_runs.py is reloaded
#   by uvicorn --reload automatically.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

